body: "# W17 SEAL — Monte Carlo Full Financial Simulation (L6.2 closure)\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-24\n**Status**: COMPLETE — composite_score 0.9967 / 1.000 PASS (threshold 0.80)\n**Predecessor**: `2026-05-24-sprint8-seal-substrate-frozen.toon` (10th — last Sprint 8 checkpoint)\n**Plan position**: 19th checkpoint in TOON hash chain\n**Closes**: L6.2 — \"Stress scenarios S01-S05 são cenários discretos; Monte Carlo full requer modelo financeiro re-executável\"\n\n## Trajectory: 6 sub-stages in 1 session\n\n| Sub-stage | Deliverable | LOC | Outputs | TOON ancestor |\n|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| **W17.0.0** | `_shared/monte_carlo_engine.py` — `truncnorm` Distribution kind | +25 patch | 8/8 invariants PASS | — |\n| **W17.0** | `_shared/cashflow_model.py` — DCF vectorized + Newton-Raphson IRR | 479 | 8/8 invariants PASS | — |\n| **W17.1** | `W17/calibrate_distributions.py` — Distribution catalog per corredor | 659 | 4 JSON outputs, 36k entries scanned | — |\n| **W17.2** | `W17/run_mc_w17.py` — MC orchestrator N=50k + Sobol Saltelli + L57+L60 fixes | 430 | 4 JSON, 44s wall-clock | — |\n| **W17.3** | `W17/voto_analytics.py` — voto-ready interpretation + MD generator | 482 | JSON + MD 13319 chars, 10 sections | — |\n| **W17.5** | `W17/validate_w17.py` — 7-invariant wave validator | 250 | composite 0.9967 PASS | — |\n| **TOTAL** | — | **~2 325** | **9 JSON + 1 MD** | this checkpoint = #11 |\n\n## The substrate built\n\n### Foundation (shared, reusable W17-W22)\n- `_shared/monte_carlo_engine.py` extended with `truncnorm` kind (was 6 → 7 kinds)\n- `_shared/cashflow_model.py` (NEW) — deterministic DCF, output_fn adapters compatible with `run_mc()`\n\n### Wave artifacts (W17/)\n- `calibrate_distributions.py` — schema-defensive reader + 10-param catalog × 3 corridors\n- `run_mc_w17.py` — orchestrator with L57 nan-safe summary + L60 Saltelli-safe Sobol recompute\n- `voto_analytics.py` — interpretive layer + MD generator honoring L21 (L4+L6+L7 sections)\n- `validate_w17.py` — 7-invariant gate\n\n### Voto-ready deliverable\n- `analise/relatoria/50500.021563_2026_16/analysis/W17_monte_carlo_full.md` (13 319 chars, 227 lines, 10 sections):\n  - SUMÁRIO EXECUTIVO + per-corridor table P(TIR<WACC)\n  - SPINE proporcionalidade\n  - 3 corridor sections with baseline + MC + tornado + S01-S05 mapping\n  - CROSS-CORRIDOR\n  - L4 Considerandos (5 itens com base regulatória)\n  - L6 Limitações (L6.2.1-L6.2.4)\n  - L7 Intertextualidade (Voto DAA 4/25, TCU 2622/13 + 2057/20 + 1901/17, Lei 8.987 + 13.448, Saltelli 2010, Brealey-Myers-Allen, Taleb)\n  - SÍNTESE PARA O VOTO\n\n## Production-validated metrics (3 real corridors)\n\n| Corredor | Baseline TIR | WACC | P(TIR<WACC) | Top Sobol ST | Veredito |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **PR-SC** | 20.03% | 10% | **0.032%** | demand_cagr 42% | ✓ aprovação técnica |\n| **Malha-Gaúcha** | 13.95% | 18% | **96.57%** | demand_cagr 47% | ⚠ outlier WACC needs review |\n| **Interestadual** | 17.90% | 10% | **0.464%** | demand_cagr 44% | ✓ aprovação técnica |\n\n**Sistêmico (independência)**: P(≥1 corredor TIR<WACC) = 96.59% (dominado por Malha-Gaúcha).\n**VPL agregado** @ WACC modal: **R$ 37.56 bi**.\n\n## Performance (production)\n\n| Stage | Time | Cost model |\n|---|---|---|\n| Calibration W17.1 | 0.14s | 36k entries scanned |\n| MC engine per corridor | 5-17s | 50k samples × 41y matrix + Saltelli (k+2)·n |\n| Sobol recompute (Malha-Gaucha) | ~10s extra | L60 fix activates on demand |\n| Voto analytics | 2.64s | 3 corridors regenerated + stress S01-S05 + MD render |\n| Validate | <1s | invariant checks |\n| **Total wall-clock** | **~47s** | well within 60s/corridor budget |\n\n## 6 new lessons (L55-L60)\n\n| # | Lesson | Domain |\n|---|---|---|\n| **L55** | Domain-realistic unit scales mandatory (TKU billions, not millions; tariff R$/TKU not R$/k_TKU) | Calibration |\n| **L56** | Sanity-check matchers: if anchored CAPEX < 50% regulatory baseline, prefer fallback (`total_marker` captures yearly sub-totals not lifetime) | Calibration |\n| **L57** | np.mean/np.std propagate NaN — needs nan-safe post-process when single sample fails Newton-Raphson | MC engine resilience |\n| **L58** | `np.bool_` not JSON serializable — cast to Python `bool()` before assigning to dict for JSON output | Python/JSON |\n| **L59** | `dataclass.to_dict()` returns fresh dict on every call — modifications to local copy don't propagate unless reference is passed explicitly | Python idiom |\n| **L60** | Saltelli `np.var(np.concatenate([yA,yB]))` propagates NaN → ALL S_i and ST_i become NaN. Fix via per-scenario validity mask across yA, yB, every yAB[i] | Sobol robustness |\n\n## L21 honored (premium voto MD generation)\n\nPer L21 (W10 v2 lesson): MD must contain EXPLICIT L4 + L6 + L7 sections, not implicit references. W17 MD has all three with anchored regulatory citations (5 considerandos in L4, 4 technical limitations in L6, 8 intertextual references in L7).\n\n## REGRA #3 honored (compose, don't modify)\n\nL57 and L60 fixes are W17-LOCAL post-process layers in `run_mc_w17.py` — `_shared/monte_carlo_engine.py` (W15.S15.4 SEALED) is UNTOUCHED except for truncnorm kind extension (additive, backward-compat).\n\n## What this unlocks\n\n| Wave | Capability unlocked by W17 |\n|---|---|\n| **W18** | Deep validation M01-M12 + C01-C23 can consume MC distribution + tornado for risk-weighting |\n| **W19** | Cross-Validation Matrix 6×6 can cite MC P(TIR<WACC) as a ROW |\n| **W20** (L6.4 closure) | Cross-Corridor TIR aggregated via Gaussian copula extends W17 stress framework |\n| **W21** | F12++/F13++/F14++/F15++ regenerate with W17 MC evidence as risk quantification |\n| **W22** (PRODUTO FINAL) | Voto v2.0 can cite tornado + percentiles + S01-S05 mapping for each corridor with full provenance chain |\n\n## SEALING STATEMENT\n\n**W17 is COMPLETE and FROZEN.**\n\nThe Monte Carlo Full Financial Simulation substrate (cashflow_model + calibrate_distributions + run_mc_w17 + voto_analytics + validate_w17) is production-ready, voto-grade, and L6.2-closing. The downstream waves W18-W22 inherit a robust quantitative-evidence layer for risk-weighted analysis and TCU-defensible voto generation. Total session time for W17: ~3h end-to-end including L57/L58/L59/L60 forensic fixes.\n\nThe next session SHOULD continue with **W18 (Deep Validation M01-M12 + C01-C23)** or **W20 (Cross-Corridor TIR Aggregated — L6.4 closure)** depending on Gabriel's priority.\n"
